{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":54639,"duration_api_ms":54639,"result":"I'll check the untracked `.orchestrator/features/` folder to see if there's a feature brief for this planning stage.The orchestrator's prompt reached me cut off after its first line, so I'll check the other agents' planning output and logs to recover the feature brief and the expected format.The orchestrator's prompt reached me cut off after its first line, so I never got the feature brief, my role, or the output format. Codex got the same cut-off prompt; its `codex.json` contains only a question asking what feature to plan. My earlier Cursor runs didn't produce a plan at all. Every one stopped at Cursor's workspace-trust prompt, so the runner needs to pass `--trust` (or `-f`).\n\nI reconstructed the feature from `claude.json` and `antigravity.json`: a `status-page` showing whether the API is up, the backend version, and the current environment. I checked their assumptions against the code. Here is my contribution in the same schema they used:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"agent\": \"cursor\",\n  \"summary\": \"Prompt arrived truncated (only the first line); feature reconstructed from sibling plans as 'status-page': a public page showing API availability, backend version and environment. My contribution is a code-grounded review of the shared contract and integration points, not a separate lane plan, since my role was not received.\",\n  \"areas_affected\": [\n    \"app/api/status/route.ts (new; no app/api routes exist today)\",\n    \"app/status/page.tsx (new)\",\n    \"proxy.ts (matcher only, optional)\",\n    \"types/index.ts\",\n    \"components/layout/Footer.tsx\",\n    \".env.example\"\n  ],\n  \"proposed_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cursor-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Freeze one contract for GET /api/status before parallel work starts. antigravity proposes a richer shape (status/services/timestamp) than claude (status/version/environment); the orchestrator