t a time; npm run verify is the gate.\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"Planning inputs are unreliable: two of four agents received a truncated prompt, so the merged plan is effectively built from two perspectives.\",\n    \"Proxy overhead on polling: /api/status goes through updateSession (auth call to Supabase) on every request unless excluded from the matcher.\",\n    \"Health check that hits Supabase on every poll can amplify load during an incident; consider a cheap query and a sane poll interval.\",\n    \"Public disclosure of environment/version (raised by claude and antigravity) still needs a user decision.\"\n  ],\n  \"tests\": [\n    \"Route handler unit test: returns the frozen shape, environment fallback to 'development', database 'mock' when Supabase is not configured.\",\n    \"Proxy test: /status and /api/status are not redirected for anonymous users.\",\n    \"UI component tests per antigravity's list (loading, operational, degraded/error, refresh).\",\n    \"Manual browser check of /status (UI change rule in AGENTS.md).\"\n  ],\n  \"questions_or_unknowns\": [\n    \"What role/lane was Cursor meant to cover? The prompt was truncated.\",\n    \"Which contract shape wins: minimal (claude) or with services/timestamp (antigravity)?\",\n    \"Public page or admin-only?\",\n    \"Should /api/status be excluded from the proxy matcher?\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nTo fix the orchestrator itself:\n1. **Truncated prompt:** It looks like a Windows argument-quoting problem, where only the text before the first newline gets through. Pass the prompt from a file or through standard input.\n2. **Trust prompt:** Add `--trust` to the Cursor agent call.\n\nThe fixes aren't verified because Ask mode limited me to reading files; I can't edit the orchestrator here. Rerun the planning stage once both are in place, so Codex and Cursor plan from the full brief.","session_id":"3871515c-ac8b-4212-a2fd-1332acf63b1f","request_id":"68c4db4e-4be9-45f1-a5a6-d30fdb1d3fdf","usage":{"inputTokens":1